      "text": "The volume of a cube is given by the formula $V = s^3$, where $s$ is the length of a side of the cube.\nTherefore, the volume of the cube with edge length six inches is $6^3 = 216$ cubic inches.\nThe volume of the cube with edge length one foot is $12^3 = 1728$ cubic inches.\nTo find the ratio of the volumes, we divide the volume of the smaller cube by the volume of the larger cube:\n$\\frac{216}{1728} = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{8}}$.\nThe answer is: \\frac{1}{8}",
